"Confirmed — workspace has nothing usable (just `.gitignore` and an empty `.kuma` dir). No prior reports, no data files, no branding assets. Full inventory below.\n\n## 1. Report Skeleton (sections, in order)\n\n| # | Section | Purpose |\n|---|---------|---------|\n| 1 | Header block | Project name, report date, period covered, author, distribution list |\n| 2 | Executive summary | 3–5 sentences: overall health, headline wins, headline risks |\n| 3 | Status dashboard | RAG tiles: overall, schedule, scope, budget, risk, quality |\n| 4 | Milestones & timeline | Key dates, status (done/on-track/at-risk/late), % complete |\n| 5 | Progress since last report | Accomplishments, with plan-vs-actual variance |\n| 6 | Upcoming work (next period) | Committed items for the next reporting window |\n| 7 | Risks & issues | Register: description, severity, likelihood, owner, mitigation, due date |\n| 8 | Decisions needed / blockers | Asks of the sponsor with a required-by date |\n| 9 | Budget & resources | Spend vs. plan, burn rate, staffing changes (if in scope) |\n| 10 | Scope & change log | Change requests: submitted/approved/rejected + impact |\n| 11 | Appendix | Glossary, links, detailed metrics |\n\n## 2. Data Points Required\n\n**Project identity**\n- Project name, project code/ID, sponsor name, PM/author name\n- Reporting period start/end, report issue date, report number (e.g., #7 of 12)\n\n**Dashboard**\n- RAG rating for each dimension + one-line justification each\n\n**Milestones**\n- 5–10 milestones: name, baseline date, forecast/actual date, status, % complete\n\n**Progress**\n- Deliverables completed this period vs. planned\n- Quantified progress metric (e.g., 42 of 60 stories, phase 2 of 4)\n\n**Risks/issues**\n- Each: title, category, severity (H/M/L), likelihood, owner, mitigation, target resolution date\n- Any risks that changed status since last report\n\n**Decisions**\n- Each: what's being asked, options considered, cost/impact of delay, decision-by date\n\n**Budget** *(optional — confirm if wanted)*\n- Budget total, spent to date, forecast at completion, variance explanation\n\n**Change log**\n- Change requests this period with status and schedule/cost impact\n\n## 3. Assets\n\n- **Branding:** company/project logo (PNG/SVG) — *none present*\n- **Color scheme:** corporate palette, or I default to a neutral professional theme\n- **Charts:** I can generate timeline/burndown/budget visuals as inline SVG from your data — no source assets needed\n- **Prior report:** useful for delta/trend comparison — *none present*\n\n## 4. Missing Inputs (the gaps)\n\n**Blocking — can't start without:**\n1. Project name + reporting period\n2. Milestone list with dates and current status\n3. Current RAG ratings (or raw facts and I'll assess them)\n\n**Important — report is thin without:**\n4. Risks/issues you already know about\n5. Decisions/asks for the sponsor\n6. Progress since last period (brain-dump acceptable)\n\n**Nice to have:**\n7. Logo/brand colors\n8. Budget figures (or skip section 9)\n9. Previous report for trend context\n10. Distribution list / confidentiality footer\n\nRaw and unorganized is fine — throw it at me in any shape and I'll structure it. Items 1–3 get a working draft; everything else slots in as provided."